From 393f123de9c55581a76248f9fa98e66b0b1b48be
Subject: macos: fix Cmd+Shift+Z redo being shadowed by Cmd+Z undo
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy_simple_text_input/commit/393f123de9c55581a76248f9fa98e66b0b1b48be
Date: 2026-06-02T00:50:24+01:00

The keyboard matcher picks the first binding whose required modifiers are
all held. Undo (KeyZ + [Super]) was listed before Redo (KeyZ + [Super,
Shift]), and Undo's modifiers are a subset of Redo's, so Cmd+Shift+Z
always resolved to Undo and Redo could never fire.

Order the Redo bindings before Undo, matching the existing Submit-before-
NewLine convention.
---
diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
index 43cce127d38086700eb61ce23958a56d5178ced6..7795c0ff0f6bb05e8394d02d23eb654e7210e156 100644
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -401,15 +401,9 @@ impl TextInputNavigationBindings {
                 TextInputAction::Paste,
                 TextInputBinding::new(KeyV, [SuperRight]),
             ),
-            (
-                TextInputAction::Undo,
-                TextInputBinding::new(KeyZ, [SuperLeft]),
-            ),
-            (
-                TextInputAction::Undo,
-                TextInputBinding::new(KeyZ, [SuperRight]),
-            ),
-            // Redo on macOS is typically Cmd+Shift+Z
+            // Redo (Cmd+Shift+Z) must come before Undo (Cmd+Z): the matcher
+            // picks the first binding whose modifiers are all held, and Undo's
+            // modifiers are a subset of Redo's.
             (
                 TextInputAction::Redo,
                 TextInputBinding::new(KeyZ, [SuperLeft, ShiftLeft]),
@@ -426,6 +420,14 @@ impl TextInputNavigationBindings {
                 TextInputAction::Redo,
                 TextInputBinding::new(KeyZ, [SuperRight, ShiftRight]),
             ),
+            (
+                TextInputAction::Undo,
+                TextInputBinding::new(KeyZ, [SuperLeft]),
+            ),
+            (
+                TextInputAction::Undo,
+                TextInputBinding::new(KeyZ, [SuperRight]),
+            ),
         ])
     }
 }
